(a) the list of villages selected from Bodoland districts and criteria adopted to select these border villages under the Vibrant Villages Programme–II (VVP-II);
(b) whether Government is aware that several strategically located villages in the Bodoland Territorial Region (BTR) along the Indo-Bhutan border remain excluded from VVP-II;
(c) whether any representation has been received from the State Government of Assam or Bodoland Territorial Region to include these left-out villages; and
(d) whether Government proposes a dynamic review or supplementary list to cover the left-out BTR villages under VVP-II?

(a) whether Government has formulated any special strategy for promoting renewable energy projects in Sixth Schedule areas;
(b) whether dedicated financial assistance has been provided to the Bodoland Territorial Region under various renewable energy schemes;
(c) the projects sanctioned during the last five years; and
(d) whether additional incentives are proposed for remote tribal areas?

(a) whether Government proposes to implement a dedicated programme for installation of rooftop solar power systems in Government schools, universities and technical institutions;
(b) whether educational institutions in the Bodoland Territorial Region, including higher educational institutions, have been covered under such initiatives;
(c) the number of institutions sanctioned; and
(d) the estimated savings in electricity expenditure and reduction in carbon emissions?

(a) whether Government is aware of the severe, recurring riverbank erosion and heavy siltation along the rivers Manas, Aie, Beki, Pagladia, and other rivers flowing from the Himalayan region, causing extensive loss of land and livelihoods in the Bodoland Territorial Region (BTR) of Assam;  
(b) the current status of the Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) and anti-erosion proposals submitted by the State Government of Assam / the Government of Bodoland Territorial Region for managing these rivers; and
(c) the timeline for providing technical appraisal, sanctioning the submitted proposals, and allocating funds for their execution under central schemes or programs?

(a) whether Government is promoting indigenous and traditional sports in the North Eastern Region (NER) and if so, the details of schemes supporting such sports in Assam;
(b) the details of projects and events implemented under the Khelo India Scheme in the State during the last three years;
(c) the number of athletes selected, trained and supported under the scheme from Bodoland Territorial Region; and
(d) how Government proposes to develop sports infrastructure and strengthen the training ecosystem across the country to meet international standards in view of Government's bid and preparations to host 2036 Olympic Games?

(a) the details of action taken by Government to ensure that the transition to the new Codes, namely, Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020 and the Code on Social Security, 2020, result in immediate compliance by tea estate owners for dues, PF, Gratuity and ESIC and all needed for protection of tea garden workers;
(b) whether Government is aware that a significant portion of the tea garden workforce remains outside the formal social security net; and
(c) if so, the roadmap to integrate these workers into national schemes like the e-Shram portal or ESIC to ensure universal coverage?

(a) details of the specific skill development, vocational, and capacity-building training programmes that have been imparted to women in Assam under the 'Samarthya' sub-scheme of Mission Shakti in the last five years;
(b) the total number of women, particularly those in distress and marginalized communities, who have benefited from these training initiatives in the State since the inception of the current Mission Shakti guidelines, details for each district;
(c) the total financial allocation made and utilized for these training components in Assam in the last five years; and
(d) details of mechanism to monitor the post-training employment?

(a) whether Government is aware of the movement of wildlife around National Highway 127C connecting Samthaibari in Assam with Galengphu near the international border with Bhutan;
(b) whether Detailed Project Report (DPR) for NH 127C take note of the site’s proximity to eco-sensitive zones, protected zones and wildlife crossings, if so, what steps were taken to ensure safe movement of wildlife along this corridor; and
(c) whether the Ministry is considering the establishment of an elevated animal corridor over specific stretches of NH127, to facilitate the safe movement of wildlife over a connected ecosystem, in accordance with guidelines outlined in IRC SP93:2017 Manual?

(a) what was the total allocation made for Assam under the National AIDS and STD Control Programme (NACP – Phase V), in each of the years from 2021 till 2026;
(b) the steps taken by the Assam AIDS Control Society under the approved action plans by the National AIDS Control Organization for prevention, surveillance, testing, awareness, capacity building in the last five years, details thereof; and
(c) the number of HIV infected individuals in Assam administered Anti-Retroviral Treatment in the last five years and the number of load tests conducted to monitor viral load suppression in the State, the details thereof?

(a) the number of development works that have been recommended under  the Members of Parliament Local Area Development Scheme (MPLADS), in districts falling under Bodoland Territorial Region (BTR) in the last five years, district-wise details, along with the total amount of the recommended works;
(b) the number of, of these recommended development works under MPLADS in districts falling under Bodoland Territorial Region (BTR) were sanctioned by the concerned implementing agency, district wise details, along with the date of sanction accorded; and
(c) the current status of each of the sanctioned developmental works in each district?

(a) whether the central Government is aware of the frequent power outages and voltage drops in the State of Assam during peak-demand seasons, particularly in lower Assam, caused by congestion on aging 132 kV transmission networks and deteriorated tower hardware;
(b) if so, steps taken for the upgradation of power transmission corridor projects in the State, including the ? 4,000 crore grid upgrade initiative and financial aid from institutions like the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB); and
(c) whether any specific timelines been set for the completion of establishment of new substations and the transition to high-capacity High Temperature Low Sag conductors?

(a) whether regular social audits are being conducted under MGNREGS, PMAY-G and DAY-NRLM in Assam;
(b) the major findings of such audits during the last five years;
(c) whether any significant irregularities have been identified in the Bodoland Territorial Region; and
(d) the corrective measures taken thereon?

J

(a) the total number of active Kisan Credit Cards (KCC) issued in Assam over the last three years, the details thereof, district-wise and category-wise including small/marginal farmers, livestock farmers and fishermen;
(b) the total amount of institutional credit that has been disbursed under KCC scheme in each of the last three years; and
(c) whether the Union Government has conducted a study to ascertain the volume of KCC loans that have fallen into the Non-Performing Assets (NPAs) category in Assam, if so, the key findings of this study?

(a) how much Grant-in-Aid has been disbursed for tribal areas in the State of Assam in last five years, under Article 275 (1) of the Indian Constitution;
(b) whether Government has taken note that the Autonomous Councils constituted under the Sixth Schedule to the Constitution have been entrusted with significant responsibilities for the protection and preservation of the identity, culture, language and traditions of tribal communities, but have limited financial resources and are largely at the mercy of their respective State Governments for funding; and
(c) whether the Ministry proposes to introduce a dedicated mechanism for financial assistance, if so, details thereof?

(a) the details regarding the financial position, accumulated losses and outstanding liabilities of fertilizer Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs) and the rationale for Government’s decision to withhold further financial assistance to loss-making units;
(b) the details regarding the status of any sector-wide assessment undertaken on the financial sustainability and demand–supply implications of creating additional fertilizer production capacity, including the ?10,600-crore fertilizer plant announced in Assam; and
(c) the details regarding the projected capacity addition, utilisation levels and expected impact on import dependence arising from the said project?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the power demand requirement of Assam upto the year 2030, if so, findings thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(b) details regarding the methodology and assumptions used for such demand projections, including factors relating to population growth, industrial expansion, urbanisation and electrification targets;
(c) details regarding the current power demand and supply in the State of Assam, including peak demand and available capacity; and
(d) details regarding ongoing power projects planned to be completed before 2030, including their current status, the name of the authority or company managing the project, and power generation capacity?

(a) whether Government has taken note of severe riverbank erosion along the rivers Manas, Aie, Beki, Pagladia, Dhansiri and Sankosh in Assam, particularly affecting the Bodoland Territorial Region; 
(b) whether any study or assessment has been conducted to evaluate the extent and impact of such riverbank erosion and if so, the details thereof; 
(c) whether any dedicated facility exists such as a quarantine centre, rescue, rehabilitation or “wildlife care zone” for injured or displaced elephants and other wild animals in Assam, particularly in the Bodoland Territorial Region; and 
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has assessed the quality of mobile and internet services in rural and semi-urban areas of Assam and other North Eastern States;
(b) the action taken against service providers for poor service quality; and
(c) the steps being taken to improve service reliability in remote areas such as Bodoland?

(a) the dropout rates at primary, upper primary and secondary levels in Assam and North East during the last five years, the reasons identified for dropout, particularly in rural and tribal areas;
(b) the measures being taken to improve retention of students, especially girls and economically weaker section; and
(c) the details of teacher training programmes conducted under centrally sponsored schemes in Assam including North East States in the last five years?

(a) whether there is any review on the number of beneficiaries covered under Ayushman Bharat – Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) in the North East specially in Bodaland Assam during the last five years, district-wise;
(b) whether there are delays in claim settlements and the steps taken to improve access and efficiency of the scheme; and
(c) the manner in which Government ensures that beneficiaries belonging to economically weaker sections receive complete and uninterrupted treatment in cases where actual cost of treatment exceeds the prescribed scheme ceiling under the AB-PMJAY and corresponding State-level health assurance schemes such as CMJAY for treatment of beneficiaries?

(a) whether Government has formulated any policy or programme to assist Guwahati city in addressing urban flooding;
(b) whether Government has taken note of the need for rejuvenation and conservation of water bodies in and around Guwahati city, including Deepor Beel, in order to enhance their carrying capacity and contribute to effective urban flood management; and
(c) whether any dedicated schemes or proposals have been formulated or implemented in this regard, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the continued instances of illegal rat-hole coal mining in some States of North East Region;
(b) the details of the action taken by Central Government, in coordination with Governments of Meghalaya and Assam respectively and other concerned agencies, to curb illegal rat-hole mining which is creating life threat to the labourers during the last three years; and
(c) whether such rat-hole mining be legalized without jeopardizing existing traditional practices and tribal laws since there is demand for coal for meeting energy demands of the nation?
